  "series": "GRAPHQL FEDERATION",
  "date": "07/09/2026",
  "slides": [
    {
      "page_title": "Why Federation Exists",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Bottleneck",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Monolith GraphQL: one schema, one owning team, merge-conflict jam",
            "Federation composes one supergraph from many deployed subgraphs",
            "Clients see one endpoint, one type system; teams ship alone",
            "BFF hand-writes stitching; federation derives it from schema metadata"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Vocabulary"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Term",
            "Means"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "subgraph",
              "service + its schema"
            ],
            [
              "supergraph",
              "composed schema + routing"
            ],
            [
              "gateway/router",
              "runtime that executes it"
            ],
            [
              "subgraph SDL",
              "the API contract"
            ],
            [
              "supergraph SDL",
              "build artifact, never hand-written"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "subgraph SDLs",
              "compose",
              "supergraph SDL",
              "router",
              "client"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Versions And Vendors"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "v1 (2019) to v2 (2022): `@shareable`, `@override`, `@interfaceObject`",
            "Apollo, GraphQL Mesh, Cosmo, Hive Gateway, Netflix DGS",
            "A spec plus directives, not one vendor product",
            "Many routers implement the same contract"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Hard Constraint",
          "items": [
            "Subgraphs never call each other's GraphQL API",
            "The gateway orchestrates every cross-service hop",
            "Breaking this rebuilds a hidden dependency graph"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Anti-Goals"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Not a general API gateway",
            "Not a caching layer",
            "Not a service mesh"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "When Not To Federate"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "One team, one deploy, fewer than two services",
            "Composition overhead outweighs the ownership win",
            "Split the monolith's teams first, then its schema"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Price Of Admission",
          "text": "A composition pipeline, a schema registry, CI schema checks, and a router sitting in the hot path of every single request."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What Makes It Federated",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A normal GraphQL server plus directives plus two root fields",
            "`_service { sdl }` returns raw SDL, directives included",
            "`_entities(representations:)` is the gateway's key lookup",
            "`@apollo/subgraph`, graphql-java, strawberry, gqlgen generate both"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "graphql",
          "lines": [
            "# reviews — same type, new fields",
            "type Product @key(fields: \"id\") {",
            "  id: ID!  reviews: [Review!]! }"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "graphql",
          "lines": [
            "# federation: logic lives in the SDL",
            "type User @key(fields: \"id\") {",
            "  id: ID!  reviews: [Review] }"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "graphql",
          "lines": [
            "# products",
            "type Product @key(fields: \"upc\") {",
            "  upc: String! name: String! price: Int! }",
            "type Query { topProducts: [Product] }"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "graphql",
          "lines": [
            "# reviews — the cross-service join",
            "type Review { body: String!",
            "  author: User  product: Product }",
            "type User @key(fields: \"id\") {",
            "  id: ID! @external  reviews: [Review] }"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Subgraphs: Anatomy Of A Service",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "graphql",
          "lines": [
            "type Query {",
            "  _service: _Service!      # raw SDL out",
            "  _entities(representations:",
            "    [_Any!]!): [_Entity]!  # key lookup",
            "}"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Generated Types"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`_Entity`: union of every local type carrying an `@key`",
            "`_Any`: scalar, untyped JSON blob",
            "Each `_Any` holds `__typename` plus the key fields"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Who Owns What"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A subgraph owns the fields it defines, never the whole type",
            "`User.email` in accounts, `User.orders` in orders",
            "`Query` and `Mutation` are implicitly shared",
            "Every subgraph may contribute root fields"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "graphql",
          "lines": [
            "# products subgraph",
            "type Product @key(fields: \"id\") {",
            "  id: ID!  name: String!  price: Int! }"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Opting Into v2"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`@link(url: \".../federation/v2.3\")` on the schema opts in",
            "`import: [\"@key\", \"@shareable\"]` names the directives you use",
            "v2: types contributable by default",
            "v1 required `extend type` in every non-owning subgraph"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Naming Discipline",
          "items": [
            "A subgraph must run and be queryable on its own",
            "Two different `User` types is a composition error",
            "Not a merge — pick one meaning, one key"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Dev Check",
          "text": "If you cannot hit the subgraph directly and get a useful answer without the router, its boundaries are wrong."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Entity, Stated Simply",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "An entity is a type identifiable across subgraph boundaries",
            "It is the unit of federation — everything joins on it",
            "`@key(fields: \"id\")` declares a uniquely identifying field set",
            "The key is a permanent public contract"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Entity or value type?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "Identity outlives the request? It is an entity",
            "No `@key`: duplicated by value in every subgraph",
            "Value types must be structurally identical to compose"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Entities And @key",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Key Shapes"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "graphql",
          "lines": [
            "@key(fields: \"id\")           # simple",
            "@key(fields: \"sku upc\")      # compound",
            "@key(fields: \"org { id } email\")  # nested",
            "@key(fields: \"id\", resolvable: false)"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Multiple keys allowed: gateway picks one the source can supply",
            "Every contributing subgraph declares a key the owner exposes",
            "`resolvable: false`: references the entity, cannot hydrate it",
            "Compound key means both fields together identify the instance"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Rules That Bite"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Choice",
            "What breaks"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "null key field",
              "runtime resolution failure"
            ],
            [
              "partial compound key",
              "representation is invalid"
            ],
            [
              "mutable key (email)",
              "caching and joins break on update"
            ],
            [
              "changed key",
              "breaks every referencing subgraph"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Nested keys need the referenced type reachable",
            "Its fields must be selectable in the referencing subgraph",
            "Otherwise composition cannot prove the path"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Interfaces"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`@interfaceObject` (v2.3+) puts a `@key` on an interface",
            "One subgraph adds fields to every implementation at once",
            "No per-implementer boilerplate in the adding subgraph"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flowchart",
          "spec": {
            "title": "Product @key(upc)",
            "rows": [
              [
                "n0"
              ],
              [
                "b0",
                "b1",
                "b2"
              ],
              [
                "c0_0",
                "c0_1",
                "c0_2"
              ],
              [
                "c1_0",
                "c1_1"
              ],
              [
                "c2_0",
                "c2_1"
              ]
            ],
            "nodes": {
              "n0": {
                "text": "Product @key(upc)",
                "shape": "diamond"
              },
              "b0": {
                "text": "products"
              },
              "b1": {
                "text": "reviews"
              },
              "b2": {
                "text": "inventory"
              },
