        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Entities And @key (cont.)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Keys Are Forever",
          "text": "Changing a key is a breaking change for every subgraph that references the type. Pick immutable identifiers on day one."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Join Implementation",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "It answers: given this key, hydrate the rest from my data",
            "Skipped entirely if the key already satisfies every field asked",
            "Returning a partial object is fine",
            "Remaining fields resolve through normal field resolvers"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "// (reference, context, info)",
            "Product: {",
            "  __resolveReference: ({ id }, ctx) =>",
            "    ctx.products.byId(id)  // null = dangling",
            "}"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Batch Or Suffer"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Gateway batches keys: one `_entities` call per subgraph per step",
            "Representations arrive as an array, not one at a time",
            "A naive per-key resolver produces N+1 database queries",
            "Fix with DataLoader keyed on the entity key, request-scoped"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "const loader = new DataLoader(ids =>",
            "  db.products.whereIn(\"id\", ids))  // 1 query",
            "// __resolveReference: ({id}) =>",
            "//   loader.load(id)"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "plan step",
              "representations[]",
              "_entities",
              "DataLoader",
              "one query"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Contract Rules"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Case",
            "Required behaviour"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "dangling ref",
              "return null, field is null, no error"
            ],
            [
              "ordering",
              "result[i] matches representation[i]"
            ],
            [
              "interface/union",
              "resolve via `__typename` in the rep"
            ],
            [
              "auth",
              "re-check per entity, query path is lost"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Resolvers run outside the original query's context path",
            "Each plan hop is one round trip plus one batch fetch",
            "Deep entity chains multiply latency, not add to it"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "cont": true
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Reference Resolvers",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Testing The Seam"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "graphql",
          "lines": [
            "{ _entities(representations: [",
            "    {__typename: \"Product\", id: \"1\"}",
            "  ]) { ... on Product { name } } }"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Contract Tests",
          "text": "Hand-write representations and call `_entities` directly. That surface, not your `Query` fields, is what the gateway actually depends on."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Core Directives",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Directive",
            "Does"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`@external`",
              "field owned elsewhere, declared for reference"
            ],
            [
              "`@requires`",
              "needs owner's fields before it can run"
            ],
            [
              "`@provides`",
              "returns a neighbour's fields inline"
            ],
            [
              "`@shareable`",
              "several subgraphs may resolve this field"
            ],
            [
              "`@override(from:)`",
              "move ownership with no downtime"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "graphql",
          "lines": [
            "weight: Int! @external",
            "dimensions: Dim @external",
            "shippingCost: Int! @requires(",
            "  fields: \"weight dimensions { l w h }\")"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`@provides` lets the planner skip a hop entirely",
            "It is an optimization only, never a source of truth",
            "Lie in a `@provides` and clients read stale or wrong data",
            "Without `@shareable`, duplicate non-key fields fail composition"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Moving Ownership"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "graphql",
          "lines": [
            "price: Int! @override(",
            "  from: \"products\",",
            "  label: \"percent(25)\")  # 25% traffic"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Progressive `@override` shifts a fraction of traffic first",
            "Watch metrics on the new owner, then raise the percentage",
            "Delete the old field only after traffic hits 100%"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Field-Level Directives",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Contracts And Interop"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Directive",
            "Purpose"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`@inaccessible`",
              "in supergraph, hidden from public API"
            ],
            [
              "`@tag(name:)`",
              "metadata for contract variants"
            ],
            [
              "`@extends`",
              "legacy v1 `extend type` marker"
            ],
            [
              "`@composeDirective`",
              "lift a custom directive to the router"
            ],
            [
              "`@interfaceObject`",
              "add fields to all implementers at once"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Build a public schema that drops `@tag(name: \"internal\")`",
            "`@inaccessible` composes but never reaches clients",
            "`@extends` still accepted for v1 interop"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "@provides",
                "lines": [
                  "Removes a hop",
                  "Must be truthful",
                  "Pure optimization"
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "@requires",
                "lines": [
                  "Adds a hop",
                  "Needs `@external` fields",
                  "Forces Sequence"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Extra Round Trip",
          "text": "Every `@requires` is fetched in its own planner step. Sprinkle five of them and you have bought five serial hops."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What Composition Is",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "N subgraph SDLs in, one supergraph SDL or an error list out",
            "Deterministic and offline — no service needs to be running",
            "`@join__` directives encode which subgraph owns which field",
            "Nobody hand-writes the supergraph, ever"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "rover supergraph compose \\",
            "  --config supergraph.yaml > super.graphql",
            "# managed federation composes in registry"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Composition: Building The Supergraph",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Errors You Will Meet"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Code",
            "Cause"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`FIELD_TYPE_MISMATCH`",
              "same field, different types"
            ],
            [
              "`INVALID_FIELD_SHARING`",
              "duplicate field, no `@shareable`"
            ],
            [
              "`KEY_FIELDS_MISSING_EXTERNAL`",
              "key the subgraph cannot satisfy"
            ],
            [
              "`SATISFIABILITY_ERROR`",
              "valid query, no execution path"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Satisfiability is the deep check, not a type-merge check",
            "It proves every possible query shape is reachable",
            "This is the guarantee stitching cannot give you"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Enum Merging",
          "items": [
            "Input-position enums intersect across subgraphs",
            "Output-position enums union across subgraphs",
            "One mismatched member can break the build"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Registry And CI"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "GraphOS, Hive, Cosmo store versions and publish the supergraph",
            "Checks run a proposed subgraph against real operation traffic",
            "Breaking changes surface in the PR, not in production"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "subgraph CI",
              "rover subgraph publish",
              "registry composes",
              "router hot-reload"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Order Of Operations"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Change",
            "Ship order"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "adding a field",
              "deploy code, then publish schema"
            ],
            [
              "removing a field",
              "publish schema, then deploy code"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "No Restart",
          "text": "The router hot-reloads a new supergraph in place. Schema change never means a gateway redeploy — that alone justifies the pipeline."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Plan, Then Execute",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Router parses the operation, plans against the supergraph, runs it",
            "Planning is a search over possible subgraph paths",
            "Scored by number of fetches and depth of the chain",
            "It is the expensive half of the router's job"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Plan node",
            "Meaning"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`Fetch`",
              "call one subgraph"
            ],
            [
              "`Sequence`",
              "ordered steps"
            ],
            [
              "`Parallel`",
              "concurrent branches"
            ],
            [
              "`Flatten`",
              "path into the response"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "caption": {
    "text": "One endpoint for clients, ten teams shipping independently — that is the whole pitch of GraphQL federation, and the bill arrives in round trips. This handbook walks the full path: subgraph anatomy, `@key` design, reference resolvers and the N+1 they hide, every field directive, composition errors decoded, how the router actually plans a query, and an honest comparison against schema stitching. Ends with a three-subgraph supergraph you can read line by line.",
